The issue might be that `get_name_in_module` doesn't receive `_HIDDEN_BUILTIN_TYPES` as extra names in the non-builtins branch. Let me look more carefully - the non-builtins branch calls `get_name_in_module(module, qualname, _HIDDEN_BUILTIN_TYPES)` which passes hidden types as extras. But the builtins branch also does the same. So both branches are identical, making the conditional redundant but not broken.

